Z||000008||Cliff Pennock||02-28-2001||05:42 PM||||The picture in the newspaper is the Tigra for sure. It's the convertible which has a more sporty look than the ordinary model (couldn't find a picture of the convertible). It's absolutely <B>not</B> the speedster. I just checked which car was introduced as the "Opel Speedster" at the Geneva Auto Show, and it's the car in the second picture.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.edmunds.com/edweb/news/Geneva99/Opel.Speedster.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.edmunds.com/edweb/news/Geneva99/Opel.Speedster.html</A>  (they even talk about the Fiero here)<BR> <A HREF="http://www.autoweb.com.au/id_HOL/doc_gmh9902101/article.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.autoweb.com.au/id_HOL/doc_gmh9902101/article.html</A> <BR>||||reg||1
